WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.340
Drone systems combine aircraft safety with account, software, communications,

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:05.500
and data security.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:09.160
Protect controller and application accounts with unique passwords and multi-factor

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:10.500
authentication where available.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.485
Remove former users and limit administrative privileges.

00:00:13.485 --> 00:00:16.500
Maintain firmware and applications through an approved process.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.720
Review significant changes before operational use and confirm settings afterward.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.110
Updates can improve security and reliability,

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:26.800
but an untested change immediately before a critical mission may create operational

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:27.685
uncertainty.

00:00:27.685 --> 00:00:31.770
Collected imagery can reveal people, homes, routines, access points, infrastructure,

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.225
or sensitive operations.

00:00:33.225 --> 00:00:36.500
Restrict access, use encrypted storage and transfer where appropriate,

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.500
and retain only what the legitimate mission and policy require.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.000
Respect privacy and property.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Notify or obtain consent where required,

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.060
avoid private areas and unnecessary identification,

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:49.001
and position sensors to collect the minimum useful data.

00:00:49.001 --> 00:00:51.985
A technically legal flight can still be intrusive or unethical.

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:55.155
Do not use drones for harassment, stalking, unlawful surveillance,

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:59.000
interference with aircraft, evasion of law enforcement, or unsafe activity.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.210
Do not bypass flight restrictions or conceal accountability.

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:05.860
Security and public-safety missions still require defined authority and proportional

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:06.500
controls.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:10.000
Ethical operation asks whether the mission is necessary, proportionate,

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.180
and explainable to affected people and accountable reviewers.

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:17.455
Protect sensitive findings, document decisions, and stop when safety, authority, privacy,

00:01:17.455 --> 00:01:19.000
or trust cannot be maintained.
